            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-07-06T06:54:32.550479+00:00",
            "notes": "## You should be really strong by Round 5. You should also have heaps of cash to splash on the really powerful items in this build!\n\nIf your other healer is able to heal most of the incoming damage quite easily, then you are in good steed to flank and play like a DPS. If not, then stay with your team, keep poking the enemies and topping up allies where you can.\n\nSome other options to discuss:\n\n- [Hyper Healer](item_108336b3-54d2-4d69-8ea4-c2da5affb7ca) is a good alternative power pick here if you're finding you need a bit more survivability or durability in your skirmishes. That extra HP is definitely something worth considering here.\n\n- [Aerial Distresser](item_0fcb9020-c729-49b9-b398-3223797b6204) is really good vs your aerial foes like Mercy, Juno and Freja. Because your DMG throughput is quite high with this build, you become a reliable anti-aerial character whilst being aerial yourself!\n\n- If you're finding that your other support can't keep up with healing and you need a little extra *oomph* then [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) is a good choice to output a bit more healing whilst not losing out on a lot of your DPS potential.\n\n- [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) can be a really good pick-up here if no one else on the team is building anti-heal. Your DoT effect let's you apply this pretty readily and can turn fights with reducing your enemy's healing potency.",
